{"path":"cpp/container/array/front.html","id":"ref-8714d74c51bff2de","name":"std::array<T,N>::front","declarations":[{"code":"reference front();","notes":"(since C++11) (constexpr since C++17)","since":"11","until":null},{"code":"const_reference front() const;","notes":"(since C++11) (constexpr since C++14)","since":"11","until":null}],"headers":["array"],"intro":"Returns a reference to the first element in the container.\n\nCalling front on an empty container causes undefined behavior.","sections":[{"title":"Parameters","text":"(none)"},{"title":"Return value","text":"Reference to the first element."},{"title":"Complexity","text":"Constant."},{"title":"Notes","text":"For a container c, the expression c.front() is equivalent to *c.begin()."}],"examples":[{"code":"#include <cassert>\n#include <array>\n\nint main() {\n    std::array<char, 4> letters{'a', 'b', 'c', 'd'};\n    assert(letters.front() == 'a');\n}","output":null,"outputKind":"Behavior demonstrated in code","unicodeEscaped":false}],"summary":"Returns a reference to the first element in the container.","source":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/array/front","introduced":"11","removed":null}
